course: dictionary
lesson: 3391
title: Expectation: what people hope for
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An expectation is a belief that something will happen, or a hope about what someone will do or be. Teachers have expectations for your work, and you may have expectations for your birthday.
explain: Context gives you clues. «The class had high expectations for the school trip.» High expectations means the teachers hoped and believed the trip would be very good. «The team won against all expectations» means nobody thought they would win.
explain: Maths uses the word too. In probability, an expectation is the average result you expect over many tries, not what happens on one try. To check a meaning, swap in «what people expected» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: An expectation is a belief that something will happen.
fact: «High expectations» means people hope or require a lot from someone.
fact: «Live up to expectations» means to do as well as people hoped.
fact: «Against all expectations» means something happened when nobody thought it would.
fact: «Below expectations» means poor, worse than it should be.
fact: In maths, expectation is the average result you expect over many tries.
exercise: «The class had high expectations for the school trip.» What does high expectations mean? | People were sure it would be cancelled | People were not allowed to go | * People hoped and believed it would be very good | People had forgotten all about it
exercise: Mia's team won «against all expectations». What does that tell us? | * Nobody thought they would win, and they did | The match was never played | Everybody knew they would win | Nobody thought they would win
exercise: Which phrase means someone did as well as people hoped? | * Live up to expectations | Against all expectations | Heartbroken expectations | Below expectations
test: In maths, what is an expectation? | The result of the very first try only | The number of people in a class | A rule that never changes | * The average result you expect over many tries
test: Which phrase means worse than it should be? | Live up to expectations | High expectations | * Below expectations | Beyond expectations
exam: What does «beyond expectations» mean? | The same as nothing at all | Worse than people hoped | * Better than people thought it would be | Very late and very slow
